WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.685
Get your f---ing hands up!

00:00:01.685 --> 00:00:02.518
What's the matter with you?

00:00:02.518 --> 00:00:04.680
Back away! Keep your hands
where I can see them!

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.692
If you're walking up and
you see a bunch of people

00:00:06.692 --> 00:00:08.933
standing in there with their hands up

00:00:08.933 --> 00:00:10.800
or laying on the ground,

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.720
first thing you're going
to do is call the police.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.000
Hi, I'm Cain Vincent Dyer.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.860
Over a period of 2 ½ years,

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.440
I did approximately
over 100 bank robberies.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.200
Today I'm back to look at
more bank-robbery scenes

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.375
in some great movies and
to judge how real it is.

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:32.580
All right, calm down.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:34.860
It is absolutely on point.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:37.110
Truck robberies are quite common.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:41.910
I think there was just one in Los Angeles

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:43.118
a week ago.

00:00:43.118 --> 00:00:45.150
They said they had taken, like, $30,000.

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:48.540
I think after review it
came down to $15,000.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:51.448
That's actually considerably small

00:00:51.448 --> 00:00:52.920
for hitting an armored car.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.690
The reason for that:

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:56.250
That's where the banks get the money from.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:59.465
With that said, you're
increasing your level of danger

00:00:59.465 --> 00:01:01.020
a hundredfold.

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:03.780
You know, those security guards

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.106
from armored car trucks

00:01:06.106 --> 00:01:08.220
are trained to shoot back
and defend that money.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.412
It's a lot different than,

00:01:09.412 --> 00:01:11.967
the thinking of a bank can typically be

00:01:11.967 --> 00:01:15.750
to let you have it and just
to get you out of there.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:18.210
Dispatcher: Any units in
the area? 1061 in progress.

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.998
I actually used police scanners

00:01:20.998 --> 00:01:25.170
in a lot of my bank heists.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:30.030
I would tap into the police
activity within an area.

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:31.140
Knowing when they're coming,

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:33.750
knowing how much time
you have left inside.

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:37.710
So, yes, it's absolutely
something that a gang

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:39.785
of that caliber would have.

00:01:42.482 --> 00:01:44.065
Let's go! Let's go!

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:51.535
We also see that they switch
cars after the robbery,

00:01:51.535 --> 00:01:54.240
which is very, very, very common.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.700
All the cars that
they're using are stolen,

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:57.780
more than likely, right?

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:59.490
Instead of stealing a car,

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:00.905
what I would do is I would find

00:02:00.905 --> 00:02:03.420
that make and model of the car that I had,

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:07.890
and I would steal the license
plate off an identical car.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:09.210
There are a lot of guys in crews

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:11.421
that are out there that are like that.

00:02:11.421 --> 00:02:13.810
You have to give "The Town" the 10.

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:15.989
What can I do you for, officer?

00:02:15.989 --> 00:02:16.920
Why are you closed?

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.690
Robber: We're going to leave one by one.

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:20.910
Nobody raise their head. Do not get up.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:25.382
I've gone into banks
yelling to take control.

00:02:25.382 --> 00:02:29.310
When I actually talk to
bank employees one-on-one

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:31.727
when I'm instructing them to do something,

00:02:31.727 --> 00:02:33.930
it's in a very soft tone.

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:37.800
That ability to adapt to a situation.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:40.128
And you see the difference between

00:02:40.128 --> 00:02:42.220
when he's in the bank
talking to the customers

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:46.703
and then when he switches his personality

00:02:46.703 --> 00:02:48.865
to deal with the police officer.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:52.284
Pig's not working, Danny.

00:02:52.284 --> 00:02:54.570
I told you this thing's a f---ing pig.

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:57.360
The car not working in that scene.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.000
You'd like to think that
you'd have a perfectly

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.390
operational vehicle when
you go do a bank robbery.

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:05.550
But, hey, things happen sometimes.

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:07.570
I actually think that is where

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:09.960
you have a lot of bank
robbers leave the car going,

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:11.550
or they'll park right in front.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:14.400
There's less effort in getting
in and starting up the car.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:15.780
They can just get in and go.

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:17.447
Let's go. Let's go. Let's go.

00:03:17.447 --> 00:03:18.352
Move, move, move, move.

00:03:18.352 --> 00:03:19.685
Get outside now!

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:21.943
Go time.

00:03:21.943 --> 00:03:23.070
F---.

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:23.903
What?

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:29.543
We see that there are undercover
police officers outside

00:03:29.543 --> 00:03:32.130
casing the bank also and waiting.

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:34.470
Years later when I turned myself in,

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:37.260
I was told that they
would actually do that.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:40.710
The special FBI agent who
was attached to my case,

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:44.040
he would put teams together,
and they would go sit

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.731
in front of banks and case banks

00:03:47.731 --> 00:03:49.489
looking for me

00:03:49.489 --> 00:03:53.610
to see if I was either casing
a bank or robbing a bank.

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:55.313
And it was all guessing work for them

00:03:55.313 --> 00:03:59.220
because I wouldn't leave too
much of a road map for them.

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:02.550
But it is something
that absolutely happens

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:05.250
when they have bigger gangs

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:07.110
that are doing multiple robberies

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:09.270
or multiple robberies have happened

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:11.250
within an area in a short time.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.050
There's a lot of special effects in there

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:16.333
and things like that,
but it's pretty accurate.

00:04:16.333 --> 00:04:17.370
I'd give it an eight.

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:18.881
Get your f---ing hands up!

00:04:18.881 --> 00:04:19.839
What's the matter with you?

00:04:19.839 --> 00:04:22.260
Back away! Keep your hands
where I can see them!

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:24.270
In so many bank robberies,

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:28.380
we actually witness the robbers coming in

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:32.574
and yelling at customers and tellers alike

00:04:32.574 --> 00:04:35.310
to get down or to raise their hands.

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:38.850
That's something that I
definitely stayed away from.

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:41.395
The thought process behind doing that

00:04:41.395 --> 00:04:46.260
is to have absolute
control of the movement.

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:49.913
I never asked anyone to lay on the floor

00:04:49.913 --> 00:04:51.180
or lift their hands.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:53.647
If you're a customer
walking up to the bank

00:04:53.647 --> 00:04:54.822
and you see a bunch of people

00:04:54.822 --> 00:04:57.030
standing in there with their hands up

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.970
or laying on the ground,
you're not going to enter.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:02.360
First thing you're going
to do is call the police.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:04.640
Hello, hello, hello, ladies and gents.

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:06.720
We are the ex-presidents!

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:10.800
We see the bank-robbery crew
wearing the president's mask,

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:12.000
the rubber mask.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.850
One of the bad things
about wearing a mask:

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:16.702
You're alerting people that probably

00:05:16.702 --> 00:05:18.720
something's going to take place here.

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:21.400
I would wear glasses and a baseball hat

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:24.617
because I wanted more so
the element of surprise

00:05:24.617 --> 00:05:27.903
and to make certain that no one saw me

00:05:27.903 --> 00:05:31.833
walking up to the bank
ready to commit a robbery.

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:34.080
Time, Mr. Carter!

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:34.913
60!

00:05:34.913 --> 00:05:36.230
Let's go, let's go, let's go!

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:38.790
In and out in 90 seconds.

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:41.610
To be in and out in a minute and a half,

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:42.930
pretty much right on the money.

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:47.230
Typically, once you go into
a bank and the alarm is set,

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:50.250
depending on where law
enforcement is in relation

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:53.820
to the bank, it'll typically
take about a minute and a half.

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:55.032
You have a group of guys

00:05:55.032 --> 00:05:57.930
that are all going after the drawers,

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:01.320
and depending on the location of the bank,

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:06.314
they're probably not leaving
with a big dollar amount.

00:06:06.314 --> 00:06:09.420
But I think their thing is quantity.

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:11.820
Do a lot of these things, get in, get out,

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:15.810
versus spending too much time
trying to take on the vault.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:17.460
But for the most part,

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:20.130
whenever you have a
group-style bank robbery,

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:23.190
it seems to be the
method that they prefer.

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:26.370
The overwhelming, the
yelling, and things like that.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:29.279
So, "Point Break," gotta give it a 10.

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:37.650
I don't know any of those
partitions that exist,

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:40.133
but I've definitely seen

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:42.908
preventative devices like that.

00:06:42.908 --> 00:06:45.394
A lot of the bulletproof windows.

00:06:45.394 --> 00:06:49.080
There's this double
doors that was created.

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:51.320
Well, the way it's set
up now in a lot of banks

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:54.328
that have been robbed a lot is

00:06:54.328 --> 00:06:58.003
once you go through that
first door on the way out,

00:06:58.003 --> 00:07:01.797
they have a mechanism that
can lock the door to outside

00:07:01.797 --> 00:07:04.468
where you actually get
stuck in the middle there.

00:07:04.468 --> 00:07:07.353
Get down, get down, get down, all of you!

00:07:07.353 --> 00:07:09.210
Get on the floor!

00:07:09.210 --> 00:07:12.960
Me personally, I never
put my hands on anyone.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:17.011
I just always felt like the minute

00:07:17.011 --> 00:07:19.310
you start assaulting people,

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:22.726
you really add a whole
nother layer of fear,

00:07:22.726 --> 00:07:26.010
which just completely
can shut someone down.

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:29.460
The biggest regret that I
actually have is, you know,

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:31.472
though I never physically harmed someone

00:07:31.472 --> 00:07:33.510
in any of the banks I did,

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:38.275
there's still a psychological toll that,

00:07:38.275 --> 00:07:42.120
of trauma, that people
absolutely can take on

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:44.640
that I didn't account for.

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:48.975
So for me, part of my penance
wasn't just turning myself in

00:07:48.975 --> 00:07:52.290
and doing a prison sentence voluntarily.

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:56.730
It was also immersing
myself in victim impact,

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:59.970
which I've done over the
years, over the last 10 years.

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:03.300
Worked with a lot of
victims of violent crime.

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:04.729
Come on! Put that in!

00:08:04.729 --> 00:08:06.062
Come on! Let's go!

00:08:06.062 --> 00:08:06.960
What about it?

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:09.735
I have definitely aborted

00:08:09.735 --> 00:08:12.480
several bank-robbery attempts.

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:16.505
One was purely instinct,

00:08:16.505 --> 00:08:18.162
and sure enough,

00:08:18.162 --> 00:08:20.863
within two minutes of me sitting there,

00:08:20.863 --> 00:08:23.190
an unmarked fed car pulled out.

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:24.540
Two federal agents got out.

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:29.460
Another time is I did have an
individual aggress towards me.

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:33.258
And since I did know that
the only way around this

00:08:33.258 --> 00:08:35.691
was going to be through a confrontation,

00:08:35.691 --> 00:08:37.516
I aborted immediately.

00:08:37.516 --> 00:08:39.960
There was just some inconsistencies there,

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:41.260
so I'm going to give it a four.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:49.800
We see them going into the
bank during a rainstorm.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:53.168
To be quite honest, those were

00:08:53.168 --> 00:08:57.450
my favorite times to
do a bank robbery. Why?

00:08:57.450 --> 00:09:01.290
Because you don't stand out
when you have on a big jacket.

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:04.740
You don't stand out if you
have a hood over your head,

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:07.665
and there's less people

00:09:07.665 --> 00:09:11.332
paying attention to things.

00:09:11.332 --> 00:09:12.787
Cellphones, cellphones, cellphones!

00:09:12.787 --> 00:09:13.865
Stay down!

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:18.720
I used to believe that
taking everybody's cellphone

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:21.068
and things like that was
kind of a waste of time,

00:09:21.068 --> 00:09:22.851
just because it would add

00:09:22.851 --> 00:09:26.251
a significant layer of timing for me.

00:09:26.251 --> 00:09:27.355
By the time they make the call,

00:09:27.355 --> 00:09:28.763
you should be in and out already.

00:09:28.763 --> 00:09:32.654
And just disguising yourself properly

00:09:32.654 --> 00:09:35.550
so they weren't capturing images of you.

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:37.860
Take a deep breath and relax.

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:40.380
We're here to rob the bank, not you.

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:43.510
We do hear him telling the customers,

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:46.470
"Hey, this is the bank's
money, not your money."

00:09:46.470 --> 00:09:50.885
I absolutely thought robbing
banks was a victimless crime

00:09:50.885 --> 00:09:54.000
because I was stealing
the institution's money,

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:57.630
not a mom-and-pop or a
store or an individual.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:00.645
Unfortunately, it's not correct thinking,

00:10:00.645 --> 00:10:02.760
just because of what I
mentioned in the past.

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:05.710
Because you don't
include someone's trauma.

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:15.510
I personally never attempted
to knock out a security system,

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:20.478
solely because what I was
doing was hitting a vault

00:10:20.478 --> 00:10:23.310
and getting out really
quick, right? In and out.

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:25.101
With that said,

00:10:25.101 --> 00:10:29.842
I have done interviews on groups

00:10:29.842 --> 00:10:32.475
that have absolutely

00:10:32.475 --> 00:10:35.391
severed security systems,

00:10:35.391 --> 00:10:38.490
built tunnels up under the bank.

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:41.478
The guys that do those
things are typically

00:10:41.478 --> 00:10:44.940
going for banks that have
multimillions of dollars.

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:48.630
I can absolutely see a crew
going about it this way.

00:10:48.630 --> 00:10:50.940
Even making some of the
mistakes that they're making,

00:10:50.940 --> 00:10:52.507
I'm going to give it about a seven.

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:55.855
All right, give me your gun, then.

00:10:55.855 --> 00:10:57.060
Everybody sit down.

00:10:57.060 --> 00:10:58.410
Everybody sit down on the floor.

00:10:58.410 --> 00:11:02.130
Deciding to hit a bank with
or without a security guard

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:03.195
is interesting to me.

00:11:03.195 --> 00:11:06.627
A lot of security guards are also trained

00:11:06.627 --> 00:11:09.270
not to react aggressively.

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:12.000
Most security guards are
there as a deterrent,

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:15.783
as a visual deterrent,
and others are there

00:11:15.783 --> 00:11:18.270
simply to be a professional witness

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:20.970
versus stopping a bank robbery.

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:23.490
Ladies behind the counter,
keep your hands visible,

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:25.020
not on the alarms, OK?

00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:28.802
We see him tell the bank employees

00:11:28.802 --> 00:11:31.560
not to sound the silent alarm.

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:34.770
It actually differs with different banks

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:37.110
and different branches,
but for the most part,

00:11:37.110 --> 00:11:40.410
those devices are usually
reserved for head tellers,

00:11:40.410 --> 00:11:42.990
managers, assistant managers.

00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:46.110
Maybe someone in an
administrative role at a desk.

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:49.380
They will hit the silent
alarm when they notice

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:51.030
you are almost on your way out,

00:11:51.030 --> 00:11:53.820
versus creating a hostage situation.

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:55.290
So it makes sense.

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:56.940
Open the gate.

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:58.560
I don't have a key.

00:11:58.560 --> 00:11:59.510
What did you say?

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:05.683
Each time I've instructed a bank manager

00:12:05.683 --> 00:12:07.241
or a head teller

00:12:07.241 --> 00:12:10.920
to take me into the vault,
they usually comply.

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:14.250
I always try to take my tone down.

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:17.280
What I was able to experience early on,

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:19.260
the more you're yelling at a person,

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:21.060
the more you're kind of flustering them.

00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:24.360
When they're under a certain
amount of pressure, they break.

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:28.440
Was he hiding the key intentionally
or did he just forget?

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:29.460
It's hard to say.

00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:31.380
It's hard to say if
they're just flustered.

00:12:31.380 --> 00:12:32.850
I'd give it around a six.

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:33.930
Jackson and I will take the vaults

00:12:33.930 --> 00:12:35.160
because we know how to use the tools.

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:36.600
You two are on crowd control.

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:39.210
Make it clear you're in charge,
or things could get messy.

00:12:39.210 --> 00:12:42.840
In this clip, we get to see
them doing a little planning

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:46.020
of what they're going to be
doing within this bank robbery.

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:49.278
I would go over every

00:12:49.278 --> 00:12:52.530
entry route, every exit.

00:12:52.530 --> 00:12:56.300
I made it my job to know
all the different routes

00:12:56.300 --> 00:12:59.793
that would get me back to my safe area.

00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:01.830
They're almost done with the vault.

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:04.740
I'd always want to be
in and out of the vault

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:07.350
in three minutes, give or take.

00:13:07.350 --> 00:13:08.760
In a situation where you have

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:11.730
a group bank heist or bank robbery,

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:14.421
it would probably be a lot easier

00:13:14.421 --> 00:13:17.297
to make entry into a vault
as long as it was open

00:13:17.297 --> 00:13:18.450
and they knew what they were doing.

00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:21.240
But if you're a lone robber like I was,

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:22.740
it could be quite risky.

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:25.681
But it is a method that I used.

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:30.420
- Cops.
- Yes!

00:13:30.420 --> 00:13:32.520
I mean, oh, no, what a bummer, the police!

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:34.920
There was a situation back in '97

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:39.780
where two off-duty officers
working in a Los Angeles bank,

00:13:39.780 --> 00:13:43.530
not in a uniform, just posing as

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:45.438
a customer within the bank,

00:13:45.438 --> 00:13:49.890
actually confronted two
bank-robbery suspects,

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:53.250
which ended up in one
of the suspects dying.

00:13:53.250 --> 00:13:57.090
But a lot of banks won't
hire armed security

00:13:57.090 --> 00:14:00.351
solely for that matter, because they know

00:14:00.351 --> 00:14:04.740
that another person inside
the bank with a firearm

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:07.350
is just more of a chance of engagement.

00:14:07.350 --> 00:14:09.900
Don't be mad at me,
"Brooklyn" fans out there.

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:11.500
I'm going to give them a two.

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:14.033
Slow down.

00:14:14.033 --> 00:14:15.530
I ain't speeding.

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:18.030
The first thing people would think,

00:14:18.030 --> 00:14:19.440
well, why are you speeding off?

00:14:19.440 --> 00:14:21.690
That is just absolute adrenaline.

00:14:21.690 --> 00:14:23.760
Once a guy told him to slow down,

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:25.380
they rolled down both windows.

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:29.040
That is something that I
actually intentionally did.

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:31.830
Typically, you would assume
someone trying to get away

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:34.290
from something, they'd be trying to be

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:36.480
as much incognito as possible.

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:37.730
That's it, come on.

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:39.960
Ah, ah, ah, no bundles.

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:40.800
Just loose cash.

00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:43.635
One of the bank robbers demanding

00:14:43.635 --> 00:14:45.720
only loose cash, no bundles.

00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:48.477
There's this belief amongst bank robbers

00:14:48.477 --> 00:14:52.620
that so much of the money
that come in bundles

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:55.290
either have dye packs that will explode

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:57.347
once you get a certain
feet away from the bank

00:14:57.347 --> 00:15:01.849
or they'll have tracers
in them, which is true.

00:15:01.849 --> 00:15:05.160
I've come across a tracer before.

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:07.890
If it's a bundle, typically
be right in the middle.

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:10.448
They believe that grabbing

00:15:10.448 --> 00:15:13.814
just loose currency

00:15:13.814 --> 00:15:16.050
would prevent them from coming across

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:18.000
a dye pack or a tracer.

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:20.760
Pretty smart, but it does
limit the money you get.

00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:21.918
Robber: Got a gun?
Customer: Yeah.

00:15:21.918 --> 00:15:23.585
Robber: Keep up with
the circumstances, OK?

00:15:23.585 --> 00:15:24.535
Customer: Yeah, I got it.

00:15:24.535 --> 00:15:26.709
So are y'all going to steal my gun too?

00:15:26.709 --> 00:15:30.600
In this scene, we see that
the customer has a firearm.

00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:34.590
That is a huge concern
amongst bank robbers.

00:15:34.590 --> 00:15:36.600
Well, at least it was for me,

00:15:36.600 --> 00:15:38.550
which is one of the reasons why,

00:15:38.550 --> 00:15:40.260
before I went into the bank,

00:15:40.260 --> 00:15:43.140
I absolutely would do my homework.

00:15:43.140 --> 00:15:46.800
I would monitor citizens
coming in out of the bank,

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:49.260
how they walked, if
they seemed aggressive,

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:52.530
if they seemed like they just
go more with the program.

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:55.623
And it's safe to say that's why I probably

00:15:55.623 --> 00:15:59.190
only had one guy come at me
within all of those robberies.

00:15:59.190 --> 00:16:01.410
Fortunately, they didn't have a weapon.

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:04.500
It's very real, with the
exception of them letting the guy

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:07.099
keep the gun, just setting
the gun on the counter.

00:16:07.099 --> 00:16:08.905
Go, run, go!

00:16:09.938 --> 00:16:11.550
Maybe we should hit that branch in Jayton.

00:16:11.550 --> 00:16:13.256
No, we ain't. We hit
those banks first thing

00:16:13.256 --> 00:16:14.356
in the f---ing morning.

00:16:14.356 --> 00:16:17.220
They robbed two banks in the same morning.

00:16:17.220 --> 00:16:18.180
I'm guilty of that.

00:16:18.180 --> 00:16:21.030
I knew one bank probably
carried a certain amount

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:22.080
during that morning,

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:25.830
and there was another
bank that was in the area.

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:27.420
They did it for a different reason.

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:30.060
It was clear their first
robbery, they didn't get a lot,

00:16:30.060 --> 00:16:33.360
so their desperation drove
them to do a second one

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:34.800
within the same day.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:37.908
That was very real.
We'll give it an eight.

